<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martinus Theunis Steyn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1857–1916</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as M. T. Steyn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martinus Theunis Steyn was a lawyer and the last president of the Orange Free State, serving from 1896 to 1902. He allied the republic with the South African Republic and led it into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a> in 1899, staying in the field with the commandos after the British occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bloemfontein">Bloemfontein</a>. He later took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a> that prepared the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martinus-theunis-steyn.jpg" alt="Martinus Theunis Steyn" width="246" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marthinus_Steyn,_Orange_Free_State_president.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
